  <title>
    <media type="image" width="40px" height="40px" its:translate="no" src="figures/orca-logo.svg" /> User extensions
  </title>
  <p>
    User extensions add personal features, commands, and settings to Orca. Install extension
    files or package directories in <code>~/.local/share/orca/extensions/</code>, or the
    corresponding location under your XDG data directory. Only install code from sources you
    trust: approved extensions run with your user account's permissions and can access content
    Orca presents, including typed text and messages.
  </p>
  <p>
    Orca does not have an official extension store. Community catalogs and stores are not
    endorsed or security-reviewed by the Orca project.
  </p>
  <p>
    Use the settings below to inspect and manage installed extensions. You can also approve or
    revoke approval from the command line, as described in "<link xref="introduction">Starting and stopping Orca</link>". Extensions
    approved that way load on the next Orca startup.
  </p>
  <section id="extension-settings">
    <title>Extension settings</title>
    <section id="settings-extension-settings">
      <title>Settings</title>
      <p>
        <em style="strong">Preferences location:</em>
        <gui>User Extensions</gui> category (global only).
      </p>
      <p>
        <em style="strong">Available settings:</em>
      </p>
      <list>
        <item>
          <p>
            <gui>User Extensions</gui>: Lists installed
            extensions. The switch beside an approved extension enables or disables it without
            removing approval. These changes take effect without restarting Orca.
          </p>
          <list>
            <item>
              <p>
                <gui>Approve</gui>: Approves the
                extension for loading after you inspect its information. Changing its contents,
                including translations in a package, invalidates approval.
              </p>
            </item>
            <item>
              <p>
                <gui>Re-approve</gui>: Approves a changed
                extension after you inspect the changes. Reapproving a disabled extension leaves
                it disabled.
              </p>
            </item>
            <item>
              <p>
                <gui>Revoke</gui>: Revokes approval and
                prevents the extension from loading. Approval changes made here take effect
                without restarting Orca.
              </p>
            </item>
            <item>
              <p>
                <gui>Delete</gui>: Removes the extension
                file or package after confirmation.
              </p>
            </item>
            <item>
              <p>
                <gui>Info</gui>: Shows extension
                information, including shortcut conflicts under "Status".
              </p>
            </item>
            <item>
              <p>
                <gui>Settings</gui>: Opens preferences
                provided by the extension. In Orca's standard extension settings dialog,
                choosing "OK" stages your changes. Apply or save the main Preferences window to
                save them.
              </p>
            </item>
          </list>
        </item>
      </list>
    </section>
  </section>
  <section id="command-shortcuts">
    <title>Command shortcuts</title>
    <p>
      An extension can load successfully even if some of its commands have no shortcut. If a
      requested shortcut is already used by an Orca command or another extension, the
      conflicting extension command is left unbound. See "<link xref="features_keyboard_layout">Keyboard layout and Orca Modifier</link>" for configuring
      shortcuts.
    </p>
  </section>
